    "description": "Rules and guidelines for swapping a skill's governing Ability Score with GM approval.",
    "body": "# Transposed Skill Base\n\nWhile every skill has a default governing Ability Score, unique character concepts, cybernetic interfaces, or psionic disciplines may justify swapping the base attribute.\n\n## Guidelines & GM Approval\n- **Permanent Transposition**: Reflects innate biological traits or heavy cybernetic links (e.g., using *Intellect* instead of *Agility* for Piloting via a neural direct-feed).\n- **Situational Transposition**: Reflects specific techniques (e.g., using *Agility* instead of *Strength* for Melee with a rapier via Weapon Finesse).\n- **Game Balance**: Must make narrative sense and cannot be used solely to min-max without corresponding character investment."
